  "prompt": "Customer service wants to know how much of the webshop's business comes in at night. A night order is a web order (channel 'web') placed at an Amsterdam hour of 22 or later, or before 6, that is, from 22:00 to 05:59 Amsterdam time. order_ts holds the time of the order in UTC: turn it into Amsterdam time first, then take the hour and the month from it. For each Amsterdam calendar month from July 2025 to December 2025 that has at least one web order, return four columns, in this order: order_month, the first day of the month as a date (such as 2025-07-01); web_orders, the number of web orders placed in that month; night_orders, the number of them that were night orders; and night_pct, 100 times night_orders divided by web_orders, rounded to 1 decimal. Sort by order_month from earliest to latest.",
  "output_contract": {
